PASS: [W10] DETECTION TEST 2 (subspace/field level, independent of the assembly code): build the tying columns from the NODE COORDINATES and the derived phase rule [W1] and test column membership. Correct column is in the space by construction; the wrong-sign column leaves a residual of squared norm 2 sin^2(theta) [W4]. Combined with TEST 3 (comparison against an independent reference at a generic interior k, where the spectra differ [W7]), this is the independent validation the ruling must preserve: no invariance of the reduced matrix can substitute for it

